WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.308
"Imitation learning for self-driving cars is
usually done through behavioral cloning,

00:00:05.388 --> 00:00:09.491
where the network is trained to reproduce an
expert's next action.

00:00:09.571 --> 00:00:15.767
The catch is that this is done open-loop: the model
never sees the consequences of its own actions.

00:00:15.847 --> 00:00:18.049
But when the policy actually drives,

00:00:18.129 --> 00:00:21.218
every action changes the future state it will see.

00:00:21.298 --> 00:00:23.436
Small prediction errors accumulate,

00:00:23.516 --> 00:00:28.698
pushing the car into out-of-distribution situations
the model was never trained on.

00:00:28.778 --> 00:00:33.452
And the metrics that truly matter, like collisions,
are non-differentiable,

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:37.508
so they are effectively invisible to the standard
training loss.

00:00:37.588 --> 00:00:43.530
The result is a policy that looks great open-loop
but drives poorly in closed-loop evaluation."
